WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.087
What are the most popular
things folks design on Canva?

00:00:04.087 --> 00:00:08.133
The range of things people design
on Canva is pretty astronomical.

00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:10.176
Presentations are really popular.

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:13.346
We've had 1 billion
presentations created recently.

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:15.098
Everything from social media graphics

00:00:15.098 --> 00:00:18.143
to marketing materials, 
videos, print products,

00:00:18.143 --> 00:00:20.145
the whole suite of products that people

00:00:20.145 --> 00:00:22.272
have now created 
15 billion designs with.

00:00:22.272 --> 00:00:25.483
200 new designs every
second. Is that right?

00:00:25.483 --> 00:00:27.235
I think that’s correct, yeah. 

00:00:27.235 --> 00:00:28.194
Pretty crazy.

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:47.088
Hi Melanie. Thank you
so much for doing this.

00:00:47.088 --> 00:00:48.423
So good to be here with you.

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:50.425
How's the weather in Sydney?

00:00:50.425 --> 00:00:51.760
It's been really lovely.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:54.971
We've had some really lovely
sunny weather for our winter.

00:00:54.971 --> 00:00:56.514
Why did you start Canva?

00:00:56.514 --> 00:00:59.059
Many years ago I was at university

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:00.810
 and I was teaching design programs

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:02.604
 and I thought they were
extraordinarily complicated.

00:01:02.604 --> 00:01:05.023
It would take a whole semester for
people to learn the very basics,

00:01:05.023 --> 00:01:07.233
and so I believed in the future 

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:08.943
everything would be
 online and collaborative

00:01:08.943 --> 00:01:10.111
 and really simple.

00:01:10.111 --> 00:01:13.156
And we've been really working
towards that now for the last decade.

00:01:13.156 --> 00:01:15.575
By we you mean 
you and your co-founders

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:16.993
and one of your co-founders I believe

00:01:16.993 --> 00:01:18.787
became your future husband, right?

00:01:18.787 --> 00:01:20.872
Yeah, well, he was actually my boyfriend

00:01:20.872 --> 00:01:23.541
before he became my co-founder, Cliff.

00:01:23.541 --> 00:01:27.587
It is quite funny looking back because
obviously over the last decade I've had

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:32.133
to learn about venture capital and angel
investors and just the whole vocabulary

00:01:32.133 --> 00:01:33.510
and the whole world.

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:35.428
 But at that point in time, we're just like,

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:36.805
let's create some software.

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:44.771
Flash forward 10 years and Canva has
been valued as high as $40 billion,

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:48.691
making it one of the world's most
valuable private software companies,

00:01:48.691 --> 00:01:50.110
but continuing to grow

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:52.987
and compete with companies 
like Adobe and Microsoft 

00:01:52.987 --> 00:01:54.781
will be no small task. 

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:56.699
And unlike other tech giants,

00:01:56.699 --> 00:01:59.953
this software company is a 
ways away from Silicon Valley. 

00:02:01.037 --> 00:02:02.122
The company's based in Sydney.

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:04.916
 Is that an advantage or a disadvantage?

00:02:04.916 --> 00:02:06.376
I think it's a massive advantage.

00:02:06.376 --> 00:02:09.337
So a vast majority of our product
work is done in Australia. 

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:12.882
We have been in
a very fortunate position

00:02:12.882 --> 00:02:15.051
 that we've been profitable
 for the last six years. 

00:02:15.051 --> 00:02:17.679
We've got 3,900 people in our team.

00:02:17.679 --> 00:02:21.182
We've been continuing to grow our
team, so we've become very global.

00:02:21.182 --> 00:02:26.271
So we're in 85% of Fortune 500's
from the HR department to the people

00:02:26.271 --> 00:02:29.107
team to marketing and sales.

00:02:29.107 --> 00:02:32.277
As I understand it, you have
a dedicated Head of Vibes?

00:02:32.277 --> 00:02:33.153
We do.

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:38.449
And you've got a 70 person team
focused on just creating a vibe.

00:02:38.449 --> 00:02:39.909
Tell me about this.

00:02:39.909 --> 00:02:41.286
Correct.

00:02:41.286 --> 00:02:42.370
I guess when we started out,

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:44.831
we always wanted to create a
company that we wanted to work at.

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:47.458
In the early days, Cliff
would make lunch for everyone,

00:02:47.458 --> 00:02:49.544
and we've just kept that rolling.

00:02:49.544 --> 00:02:51.880
And so now we've got 
almost 4,000 people

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:54.549
and obviously Cliff can't
 make lunch for everyone.

00:02:54.549 --> 00:02:59.179
So we've got 70 amazing
people in our Vibe team 

00:02:59.179 --> 00:03:03.850
who they help create celebrations and 
they help create team bonding events

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.727
 and they help create
 the office environment

00:03:05.727 --> 00:03:08.980
and vibe to keep everyone together

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:10.064
and feeling great.

00:03:10.064 --> 00:03:15.236
Do you think of Canva as an antidote
to the sort of stereotypical tech bro

00:03:15.236 --> 00:03:16.613
culture of Silicon Valley?

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:22.243
I dunno. I've just always
focused on doing it our way,

00:03:22.243 --> 00:03:24.621
doing it the way that makes sense for us.

00:03:24.621 --> 00:03:26.039
If that's an antidote,

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:27.457
 I mean, so be it.

00:03:27.457 --> 00:03:29.334
Let's talk about AI. 

00:03:29.334 --> 00:03:31.920
What is Canva's AI strategy?

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:32.962
The whole premise of Canva 

00:03:32.962 --> 00:03:35.673
was to make design simpler 
and easier for everyone.

00:03:35.673 --> 00:03:36.841
That was the genesis,

00:03:36.841 --> 00:03:41.763
and we're in a really fortunate position
that AI just really accelerates that.

00:03:41.763 --> 00:03:45.308
And so we have been 
deeply embedding AI 

00:03:45.308 --> 00:03:47.060
across the entirety of our visual suite. 

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:51.439
So inside our products, you can
now use generative AI to create content.

00:03:52.815 --> 00:03:56.027
You can edit a photo 
and add something in.

00:03:56.027 --> 00:03:56.945
Do you want me to show you?

00:03:56.945 --> 00:03:57.612
 Yeah. 

00:03:57.612 --> 00:03:59.197
Let's do it. OK,

00:03:59.197 --> 00:04:02.492
I'll share you this link so
we can collaborate together

00:04:02.492 --> 00:04:04.661
and then I'll show you 
some magic features.

00:04:04.661 --> 00:04:08.414
It pops up all these different
templates that you can choose from.

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:11.751
Should we do a presentation
on AI and software?

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:14.587
AI and software? 

00:04:15.838 --> 00:04:16.923
Wow. That was fast.

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:21.135
And then you can come here and you
can replace anything that you like.

00:04:21.135 --> 00:04:23.930
Let's get a picture of San Francisco

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:26.140
and you can just drag and drop

00:04:26.140 --> 00:04:28.476
and place it onto your page.

00:04:28.476 --> 00:04:29.769
 There we go.

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:30.853
Beautiful.

00:04:30.853 --> 00:04:33.398
What would you like in the water?

00:04:33.398 --> 00:04:34.274
Dolphins.

00:04:34.274 --> 00:04:36.359
Oh, dolphins. Yeah, let's do that. 

00:04:37.777 --> 00:04:41.823
Wow, that's crazy. Cool.

00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:44.826
When Canva first came onto the scene,

00:04:44.826 --> 00:04:47.287
it had an immediate edge 
over software giants 

00:04:47.287 --> 00:04:50.373
by appealing to more casual users.

00:04:50.373 --> 00:04:51.582
But now Adobe,

00:04:51.582 --> 00:04:53.918
longtime, a top seller 
of creative software

00:04:53.918 --> 00:04:57.213
 has had time to catch up 
with competing user-friendly tools, 

00:04:57.213 --> 00:04:58.673
plans to buy Figma, 

00:04:58.673 --> 00:05:00.675
a global web design platform,

00:05:00.675 --> 00:05:04.262
and its investments in generative AI.

00:05:04.262 --> 00:05:06.180
What makes you think
 you can beat them?

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:08.474
I think there was a
huge gap in the market,

00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:10.226
and so it's not necessarily competing,

00:05:10.226 --> 00:05:13.730
but creating something that filled a
gap that people really experienced.

00:05:13.730 --> 00:05:17.483
You sort of have Microsoft
on one side, which was very

00:05:17.483 --> 00:05:19.527
not necessarily very beautiful,

00:05:19.527 --> 00:05:20.945
 and then you'd have
 Adobe on the other side.

00:05:20.945 --> 00:05:22.572
That was very complicated,

00:05:22.572 --> 00:05:23.948
and we saw this gap in the middle

00:05:23.948 --> 00:05:26.075
 where people wanted to design something really great

00:05:26.075 --> 00:05:29.370
 to express their concepts
and to achieve their goals,

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:33.374
but they didn't necessarily have years
to invest in learning the tools. 

00:05:33.374 --> 00:05:35.710
And then with Canva, 
obviously we've just done

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:37.754
use this same platform,

00:05:37.754 --> 00:05:40.715
so you can design each of these
different things with the same ease.

00:05:40.715 --> 00:05:44.093
So you can design a presentation as
easily as you can design a website.

00:05:46.596 --> 00:05:49.599
I think something that we're really
excited about is combining all of these

00:05:49.599 --> 00:05:51.184
different aspects together,

00:05:51.184 --> 00:05:53.144
and we think that we are
in a great position to help

00:05:53.144 --> 00:05:54.687
do this dance where we take

00:05:54.687 --> 00:05:57.857
technology and we take creativity and
we combine them together.

00:05:57.857 --> 00:05:59.567
Because AI does a 
great job at some things,

00:05:59.567 --> 00:06:00.902
 but not other things.

00:06:00.902 --> 00:06:02.528
Like creating a really authentic image

00:06:02.528 --> 00:06:04.614
is something that AI 
does not do a great job of.

00:06:04.614 --> 00:06:06.032
So combining them together

00:06:06.032 --> 00:06:07.867
 to help people achieve their goals

00:06:07.867 --> 00:06:09.452
is very much where we're focused 

00:06:09.452 --> 00:06:12.330
and we're extraordinarily
excited to create the magic

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:13.873
 over the next decade.

00:06:13.873 --> 00:06:17.710
Well, here's to try and make
more magic. We'll be watching.

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:18.419
 Thank you so much, Emily.

00:06:18.419 --> 00:06:19.712
 Lovely to chat with you.

